# 1️⃣ CSS Basics

## What is CSS?

CSS controls how HTML elements look.

HTML:

```html
<h1>Hello World</h1>
```

CSS:

```css
h1 {
    color: blue;
    font-size: 40px;
}
```

Result:

```text
Hello World
```

The HTML creates the content.

The CSS controls the appearance.

---

# 2️⃣ Connecting CSS to HTML

Create:

```text
css/style.css
```

Then add this inside the `<head>`:

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="css/style.css">
```

Example:

```html
<head>

    <title>My Website</title>

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/style.css">

</head>
```

Every HTML page should use the stylesheet.

---

# 3️⃣ CSS Selectors

## Element Selector

```css
h1 {
    color: blue;
}
```

This applies to every `<h1>`.

---

## Class Selector

HTML:

```html
<h1 class="title">
    My Website
</h1>
```

CSS:

```css
.title {
    color: blue;
}
```

Classes are useful when multiple elements need the same styling.

